  body: "rmw3 authorized (ii) before vsf-rsi production: build scenario-memory to close autonomy C6. Implemented the core learning substrate (phase 1: observation/record + retrieval) in Python under child/scripts/vsl/ (auditable by the same gate). Promoted autonomy-cert C6 from a static linkage check to a DYNAMIC runtime drill that actually records a cert result and matches a novel fault to the prior correction path.",
  root_cause: "C6 (scenario_learns) was the only unclosed autonomy criterion; it needs a real, running substrate, not a doc link.",
  fix: "scripts/vsl/scenario_memory.py: record(decision,outcome,correction_path) -> stable id; match(fault_signature) -> (id,path) or None (UNKNOWN, never hallucinated); validate_store() flags corrupted/forged records. tests/test_scenario_memory.py: 4 negative-control tests (record+retrieve, unseen->UNKNOWN, corrupted rejected, garbage rejected). check_autonomy_cert.c6() now dynamically loads scenario_memory, sandboxes its store, records a cert, asserts retrieval + UNKNOWN-on-unseen. spec + plan updated (status implementing; source_spec includes the .py).",
  lesson: "The autonomy loop is not closed by a citation — it is closed by code that runs and is itself drilled (C6 dynamic). A 'learning system' that only links docs is a declaration; one that records+matches under adversarial test is action.",
  references: ["scripts/vsl/scenario_memory.py", "tests/test_scenario_memory.py", "scripts/vsl/check_autonomy_cert.py", "docs/scenario_memory_spec.vsm"],
}
